{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Cause CONFIRMED — and the prime suspect (2645 / 25d1d683e55a) is REFUTED\n\n**The prime suspect is refuted.** `25d1d683e55a` (\"Add probe_source Terraform grounding tool\")\ndid NOT modify the failing test. `git show 25d1d683e55a -- tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py`\nis +17/-0 and adds exactly one NEW test (`test_code_review_provider_advertises_probe_source_as_third_tool`)\nplus a `_TF_TOOLS_ALL` constant. It does not touch\n`test_ac3_verifier_routing_gets_distinct_fresh_terraform_session` at all. Its production diff\n(`terraform_tools.py`, `terraform_seam.py`) adds a third tool and drops an unused `_location`\nparameter; it changes NOTHING about session lifecycle or routing. The timeline fit was\ncoincidence.\n\n**The actual cause is the test's own measurement, and the failure is a FLAKE that predates 2645.**\nThe test recorded `id(session)` for each opened session:\n\n```python\nopened.append(id(session))\n...\nassert len(opened) >= 2 and len(set(opened[:2])) == 2\n```\n\nThe IaC pass's session is dropped before the verify pass opens its own — nothing retains it,\nbecause only the integer `id()` was kept. CPython recycles the address of a freed object, so two\ngenuinely distinct sessions can report the same `id()`. `1 == 2` is an allocator artifact, not a\nrouting defect.\n\n### Reproduction, with the extra installed (AC1)\n\n`python-hcl2==8.1.3` (the `grounding-terraform` extra) installed into the worktree venv; test\nconfirmed EXECUTING, not skipping (6-10 s runtime, versus the 3.86 s skip in the ticket).\n\n- 8 runs: 1 failure. 12 further runs: 1 failure. Roughly 12%.\n- The captured failure is byte-identical to CI: `E assert (2 >= 2 and 1 == 2)` at the\n  `len(set(opened[:2])) == 2` line.\n\n### Proof the routing is CORRECT and only the measurement was wrong (AC2)\n\nA probe variant that holds a STRONG reference to each session (so no address can be recycled) and\ncompares by identity ran 10/10 green, printing distinct addresses every time:\n\n```\nPROBE distinct-objs: True ids: [4499179184, 4486049584]\nPROBE distinct-objs: True ids: [4530306944, 4530785072]\n... (10/10)\n```\n\nSeparately, plain CPython demonstrates the recycling directly: three sequentially-allocated and\nfreed objects returned `distinct: 1` — one id for three objects.\n\nSo the production contract holds: `_open_session_tools` calls `tft.open_session` once per routed\ncall, and the IaC and verify passes always receive two distinct fresh sessions.\n\n### Which side is fixed, and why (AC4)\n\n**The test is fixed, not the code — and the assertion is STRENGTHENED, not relaxed.** The old\ncontract (\"verifier routing gets a distinct fresh terraform session\") is unchanged and still fully\nenforced; only the way it is measured changes. `id()` on objects whose lifetimes do not overlap is\nnot a valid identity token, so the old check was an unsound proxy that could report a false\nfailure (and, symmetrically, could have hidden a real one). Holding the session objects and\nasserting `opened[0] is not opened[1]` tests the same contract soundly.\n\n### Seeded-defect evidence (the fixed test still catches a REAL regression)\n\nA genuine session-reuse defect was seeded into `_open_session_tools` (module-level cache so both\npasses share one session). The fixed test FAILED 3/3 — deterministically, where the old\n`id()`-based test would have been unreliable. The seam was then restored and\n`git diff -- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/terraform_seam.py` is empty.\n\n### Verification\n\n- Fixed test: 0 failures in 25 runs (baseline ~12%).\n- Whole file `tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py`: 13 passed.\n- `make lint` exit 0; complexity ratchet `new=0 increased=0`; mechanism ratchet\n  `new=0 increased=0`; `make typecheck` clean (764 files).\n\n### Sweep lanes (AC5)\n\n`macos full suite`, `py3.15`, `py3.14t` are **DIFFERENT-cause** — all three fail identically on\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_reconciler_apply_bindings.py::test_reconcile_once_threads_composed_runtime_transport_into_apply`\n(`assert None is namespace(name='composed-transport')`), a different subsystem and a deterministic\nfailure rather than this ~12% flake. Filed separately as `ae96-72a9-8145-4c85`\n(`primordial-ardent-zethuswasp`), linked `discovered_from` this ticket. `sweep (windows)` is\n`continue-on-error` and left to the Windows epic.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788596821992553035,"uuid":"fc1c4b93-bc74-47a7-8352-7b3b854824af"}